---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
import DemoScript from '../../../../components/DemoScript.astro';
---

<p>
  Some answers read better as a few numbers, a chart or a table than as a paragraph. The assistant
  returns them as JSON nodes, and <code>wc-generative-view</code> lays them out with Peacock
  components (ADR-030002). The numbers come from the platform; the model only chooses how to show
  them. Press a bar, a row or a button: each fires <code>action</code> with the node's id, and the
  view does nothing else.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-generative-view id='generative-demo' label='Incidents this week' style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 44rem;'></wc-generative-view>
  <script is:inline src='/assets/js/generative-demo.js'></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var view = document.querySelector('#generative-demo');
      view.citations = window.peacockGenerativeDemo.citations;
      view.value = window.peacockGenerativeDemo.answer;
      view.addEventListener('action', function (event) {
        myConsole.log('action: ' + JSON.stringify(event.detail));
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>

<DemoScript name='generative-demo' />

<h3>Nodes</h3>
<p>
  A node is <code>{"type", "props", "children", "slot", "action", "payload"}</code>. <code>type</code>
  is a component of the catalog, such as <code>stat</code>, <code>chart-bar</code> or
  <code>table</code>, or <code>text</code> for a heading or paragraph. Children are nodes or plain
  text, never HTML; a child with <code>slot</code> goes in that named slot, such as a stat's
  <code>insight</code>. A card puts its children in padded content.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-generative-view
    style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 22rem;'
    hide-badge
    value={JSON.stringify({
      type: 'card',
      props: { variant: 'outlined' },
      children: [
        { type: 'stat', props: { label: 'Your open requests', value: 4, previous: 2, variant: 'plain' }, children: [
          { type: 'markdown', slot: 'insight', props: { size: 'sm', value: 'Two are waiting on **Ada Lovelace**.' } },
        ] },
        { type: 'button', props: { level: 'secondary', size: 'sm' }, action: 'open-requests', children: ['See them'] },
      ],
    })}
  ></wc-generative-view>
</DemoComponentCard>

<h3>What it refuses</h3>
<p>
  Model text is untrusted, so the view renders only what its catalog allows, and
  <code>issues</code> lists what it dropped. There is no HTML, no <code>href</code> or
  <code>src</code>, no callback; an unknown node shows as its text, an unknown or ill-typed prop is
  dropped, icon names are plain names, colors are plain colors or tokens, and the tree stops at 12
  levels and 500 nodes. Below, an answer with an <code>iframe</code>, a link and an HTML string: only
  the text and the button's label survive.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-generative-view
    id='generative-refuse'
    style='inline-size: 100%; max-inline-size: 30rem;'
    value={JSON.stringify([
      '<img src=x onerror="alert(1)"> is shown as text.',
      { type: 'iframe', props: { src: 'https://example.com' }, children: ['An unknown node shows its text.'] },
      { type: 'button', props: { href: 'https://example.com', level: 'primary' }, children: ['No link'] },
    ])}
  ></wc-generative-view>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var view = document.querySelector('#generative-refuse');
      customElements.whenDefined('wc-generative-view').then(function () {
        return view.updateComplete;
      }).then(function () {
        view.issues.forEach(function (issue) {
          myConsole.log('issue: ' + issue);
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>
</DemoComponentCard>
